{
  "_comment": "The quiz's only source of words. Questions are generated from this at run time, never stored. `category` makes a wrong option plausible (same topic); `sense` makes it safe (two entries sharing a sense can never appear in the same question, so no two options can be defensibly correct). `en` is the single commonly understood meaning, not a list of shades.",
  "dialect": "Modern Standard Arabic",
  "_dialect_comment": "One dialect only, shown beside the question so you know which Arabic is being asked for. No word here occurs anywhere in the Qur'an, not in the 385-word book list, not in the corpus; so the Everyday set and the Qur'anic set never overlap and nothing is filtered at run time. That rule is what shapes the topics: bread, dog and star are all Qur'anic, so what is left is modern life; work, school, health, travel, the city, technology.",
  "_categories_comment": "Every topic in the list, and what kind of word it holds. The kind is what keeps a question fair: a wrong option that is a verb beside a noun answer is dismissed on grammar alone, without reading the Arabic. Words the topic gets wrong are corrected one at a time in backend/data/word_kinds.json.",
